nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, the @SJ is very dubious and should be discounted. Additionally the hand contains 4 “quacks” (queens and jacks) and no aces or tens which, according to Bergen Hand Evaluation, means you should deduct a point. So pass is clearly best.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Generally, you strain to preempt in 3rd seat, and it would not be totally out of the question to open 2@H because of the wonderful distribution. However, I think despite 3rd seat and the distribution, pass is best.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It would be interested to see what happens if I bid 2@H. I might end up in 2@H doubled which probably does not fare well.|
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BEast: ^*NThe other thing about my passing, rule of 20 aside, was ace less hand and my longest suit is just awful.|
PG| ***** 5 ***** |


