nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally I play you should use |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| when competing. That means since West knows their side has 9 hearts, 3@H is a reasonable bid but, with 4-3-3-3 I deduct one from the normal |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| calculation. Plus vulnerable against not vulnerable, 3@H is very dangerous. So I think I pass or bid 2@H at best.|
